{"module":"lawmaking","voice":"female","duration":169.3,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"How a bill becomes law, and how this one could","start":0.0,"end":3.44,"words":[[0.05,0.32],[0.32,0.5],[0.5,0.77],[0.77,1.31],[1.31,1.57],[1.89,2.16],[2.16,2.43],[2.43,2.69],[2.69,2.96],[2.96,3.23]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Most people have never watched a bill move.","start":4.24,"end":7.13,"words":[[4.3,4.67],[4.67,5.05],[5.05,5.27],[5.27,5.57],[5.57,5.95],[5.95,6.1],[6.1,6.32],[6.32,6.62]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Knowing the steps tells you exactly where your call, letter or visit can make a difference.","start":7.48,"end":12.93,"words":[[7.54,7.91],[7.91,8.05],[8.05,8.42],[8.42,8.72],[8.72,8.86],[8.86,9.45],[9.45,9.68],[9.68,9.82],[9.82,10.12],[10.38,10.67],[10.67,10.74],[10.74,11.11],[11.11,11.33],[11.33,11.63],[11.63,11.78],[11.78,12.37]]},{"el":"h0","text":"The steps","start":13.28,"end":14.32,"words":[[13.33,13.58],[13.58,14.2]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A member of the House or Senate introduces a bill, often with cosponsors, and it is referred to a committee: a CAREN Act would go to the House and Senate Judiciary Committees.","start":15.02,"end":25.12,"words":[[15.07,15.21],[15.21,15.56],[15.56,15.69],[15.69,15.83],[15.83,16.11],[16.11,16.18],[16.18,16.53],[16.53,17.3],[17.3,17.44],[17.44,17.72],[17.96,18.24],[18.24,18.45],[18.45,19.15],[19.39,19.6],[19.6,19.74],[19.74,19.88],[19.88,20.23],[20.23,20.37],[20.37,20.51],[20.51,20.99],[21.24,21.38],[21.38,21.73],[21.73,21.94],[21.94,22.15],[22.15,22.35],[22.35,22.49],[22.49,22.63],[22.63,22.91],[22.91,23.12],[23.12,23.47],[23.47,24.1],[24.1,24.66]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The committee chair decides whether to hold a hearing and a “markup,” where members debate and amend it.","start":25.47,"end":31.42,"words":[[25.52,25.66],[25.66,26.1],[26.1,26.38],[26.38,26.89],[26.89,27.18],[27.18,27.32],[27.32,27.68],[27.68,27.83],[27.83,28.26],[28.26,28.48],[28.48,28.62],[28.62,29.06],[29.06,29.27],[29.27,29.71],[29.71,30.14],[30.14,30.36],[30.36,30.72],[30.72,30.93]]},{"el":"s0","text":"If the committee approves it, leaders decide whether it gets a floor vote.","start":31.77,"end":35.84,"words":[[31.82,31.96],[31.96,32.09],[32.09,32.49],[32.49,32.89],[32.89,33.09],[33.33,33.66],[33.66,34.06],[34.06,34.33],[34.33,34.46],[34.46,34.73],[34.73,34.87],[34.87,35.07],[35.07,35.4]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In the Senate, most bills need 60 votes to end debate (the filibuster).","start":36.19,"end":40.85,"words":[[36.24,36.38],[36.38,36.52],[36.52,36.93],[37.18,37.53],[37.53,37.8],[37.8,38.01],[38.01,38.43],[38.43,38.78],[38.78,38.92],[38.92,39.13],[39.13,39.54],[39.54,39.68],[39.68,40.38]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Both chambers must pass identical text, and the president signs it or vetoes it; Congress can override a veto with two-thirds of each chamber.","start":41.2,"end":50.21,"words":[[41.25,41.54],[41.54,42.1],[42.1,42.38],[42.38,42.59],[42.59,43.29],[43.29,43.71],[43.96,44.17],[44.17,44.31],[44.31,44.94],[44.94,45.29],[45.29,45.43],[45.43,45.5],[45.5,45.93],[45.93,46.14],[46.38,46.87],[46.87,47.08],[47.08,47.65],[47.65,47.79],[47.79,48.14],[48.14,48.35],[48.35,48.77],[48.77,48.91],[48.91,49.12],[49.12,49.68]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Why most bills die","start":51.11,"end":52.7,"words":[[51.16,51.45],[51.45,51.91],[51.91,52.29],[52.29,52.57]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In recent Congresses, only a few percent of bills introduced became law (GovTrack).","start":53.4,"end":58.71,"words":[[53.45,53.59],[53.59,54.01],[54.01,54.71],[54.95,55.3],[55.3,55.44],[55.44,55.64],[55.64,56.06],[56.06,56.2],[56.2,56.48],[56.48,57.17],[57.17,57.59],[57.59,57.73],[57.73,58.29]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Most never get a hearing.","start":59.06,"end":60.64,"words":[[59.11,59.38],[59.38,59.6],[59.6,59.76],[59.76,59.87],[59.87,60.25]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Every bill that hasn't passed dies when a Congress ends and must be reintroduced; the 120th Congress begins on January 3, 2027.","start":60.99,"end":71.02,"words":[[61.04,61.31],[61.31,61.52],[61.52,61.73],[61.73,62.14],[62.14,62.42],[62.42,62.69],[62.69,62.9],[62.9,63.04],[63.04,63.52],[63.52,63.8],[63.8,64.0],[64.0,64.28],[64.28,64.42],[64.42,65.38],[65.62,65.76],[65.76,67.14],[67.14,67.62],[67.62,68.04],[68.04,68.17],[68.17,68.79],[68.79,69.07],[69.31,70.55]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The bills that move usually have a committee champion, cosponsors from both parties, outside endorsements, and constituents in key districts asking for them.","start":71.37,"end":81.62,"words":[[71.42,71.57],[71.57,71.87],[71.87,72.09],[72.09,72.31],[72.31,72.83],[72.83,73.06],[73.06,73.21],[73.21,73.65],[73.65,74.32],[74.58,75.25],[75.25,75.55],[75.55,75.85],[75.85,76.29],[76.55,77.07],[77.07,77.89],[78.15,78.37],[78.37,79.34],[79.34,79.49],[79.49,79.64],[79.64,80.31],[80.31,80.68],[80.68,80.83],[80.83,81.13]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Other ways a bill moves","start":82.52,"end":84.38,"words":[[82.57,82.89],[82.89,83.31],[83.31,83.52],[83.52,83.84],[83.84,84.26]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Small bills often pass by being folded into larger ones, such as a broader policing or civil rights package, or attached as an amendment.","start":85.08,"end":94.31,"words":[[85.12,85.43],[85.43,85.75],[85.75,86.06],[86.06,86.3],[86.3,86.53],[86.53,86.92],[86.92,87.47],[87.47,87.79],[87.79,88.18],[88.18,88.57],[88.84,89.16],[89.16,89.32],[89.32,89.47],[89.47,89.86],[89.86,90.41],[90.41,90.49],[90.49,90.88],[90.88,91.28],[91.28,91.83],[92.1,92.18],[92.18,92.65],[92.65,92.81],[92.81,92.96],[92.96,93.75]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A “companion” bill introduced in the other chamber lets both move at once.","start":94.66,"end":98.97,"words":[[94.7,94.83],[94.83,95.44],[95.44,95.64],[95.64,96.3],[96.3,96.44],[96.44,96.57],[96.57,96.77],[96.77,97.24],[97.24,97.51],[97.51,97.78],[97.78,97.98],[97.98,98.11],[98.11,98.45]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Hearings can also be requested on an issue, which builds a record even before a vote.","start":99.32,"end":104.7,"words":[[99.33,99.83],[99.83,100.04],[100.04,100.4],[100.4,100.54],[100.54,101.18],[101.18,101.33],[101.33,101.47],[101.47,101.75],[102.0,102.29],[102.29,102.65],[102.65,102.79],[102.79,103.15],[103.15,103.43],[103.43,103.72],[103.72,103.86],[103.86,104.22]]},{"el":"h3","text":"States move first","start":105.6,"end":107.36,"words":[[105.65,106.39],[106.39,106.76],[106.76,107.25]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Federal laws often follow state ones.","start":108.06,"end":110.9,"words":[[108.11,108.65],[108.65,108.89],[108.89,109.2],[109.2,109.59],[109.59,109.98],[109.98,110.37]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Oregon passed its law against racially biased police calls in 2019 after a lawmaker shared her own experience; California, New York and the city of San Francisco followed in 2020.","start":111.25,"end":123.65,"words":[[111.29,111.73],[111.73,112.03],[112.03,112.25],[112.25,112.4],[112.4,112.84],[112.84,113.35],[113.35,113.79],[113.79,114.16],[114.16,114.46],[114.46,114.6],[114.6,115.56],[115.56,115.86],[115.86,116.0],[116.0,116.52],[116.52,116.81],[116.81,116.96],[116.96,117.18],[117.18,118.14],[118.4,119.13],[119.39,119.61],[119.61,119.83],[119.83,120.05],[120.05,120.2],[120.2,120.49],[120.49,120.64],[120.64,120.86],[120.86,121.6],[121.6,122.04],[122.04,122.19],[122.19,123.15]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Each state law shows Congress the idea works and gives members a model.","start":124.0,"end":128.23,"words":[[124.06,124.27],[124.27,124.62],[124.62,124.76],[124.76,125.04],[125.04,125.53],[125.53,125.67],[125.67,126.02],[126.02,126.3],[126.3,126.51],[126.51,126.79],[126.79,127.21],[127.21,127.35],[127.35,127.77]]},{"el":"h4","text":"A path for a federal CAREN Act","start":129.13,"end":131.83,"words":[[129.18,129.39],[129.39,129.71],[129.71,129.92],[129.92,130.14],[130.14,130.89],[130.89,131.42],[131.42,131.74]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Find a House sponsor on the Judiciary Committee, and a Senate sponsor for a companion bill.","start":132.53,"end":137.79,"words":[[132.59,132.92],[132.92,133.05],[133.05,133.31],[133.31,133.7],[133.7,133.83],[133.83,133.96],[133.96,134.54],[134.54,135.0],[135.23,135.42],[135.42,135.55],[135.55,135.88],[135.88,136.27],[136.27,136.4],[136.4,136.53],[136.53,137.11],[137.11,137.37]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The map's allies layer shows committee members.","start":138.14,"end":141.18,"words":[[138.19,138.34],[138.34,138.64],[138.64,139.02],[139.02,139.32],[139.32,139.62],[139.62,140.07],[140.07,140.6]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Gather cosponsors from both parties.","start":141.53,"end":144.1,"words":[[141.58,141.87],[141.87,142.52],[142.52,142.81],[142.81,143.1],[143.1,143.53]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Ask your own members directly.","start":144.45,"end":146.41,"words":[[144.5,144.68],[144.68,144.81],[144.81,144.99],[144.99,145.36],[145.36,145.97]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Line up endorsements from civil rights, faith, law enforcement reform and business groups.","start":146.76,"end":153.4,"words":[[146.81,147.14],[147.14,147.3],[147.3,148.13],[148.13,148.46],[148.46,148.87],[148.87,149.36],[149.65,150.06],[150.35,150.51],[150.51,151.25],[151.25,151.66],[151.66,151.91],[151.91,152.4],[152.4,152.9]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Build the record: stories, 911 outcome data and city and state resolutions (toolkit).","start":153.75,"end":159.84,"words":[[153.8,154.06],[154.06,154.18],[154.18,154.56],[154.78,155.23],[155.45,156.66],[156.66,157.04],[157.04,157.35],[157.35,157.54],[157.54,157.8],[157.8,157.99],[157.99,158.3],[158.3,158.94],[158.94,159.38]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Ask for a hearing, or for the bill to be included in a larger package.","start":160.19,"end":164.53,"words":[[160.24,160.45],[160.45,160.59],[160.59,160.73],[160.73,161.23],[161.47,161.54],[161.54,161.69],[161.69,161.83],[161.83,162.04],[162.04,162.18],[162.18,162.32],[162.32,162.89],[162.89,163.03],[163.03,163.17],[163.17,163.53],[163.53,164.02]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Keep going in the states so the pressure grows from below.","start":164.88,"end":168.42,"words":[[164.88,165.09],[165.09,165.44],[165.44,165.58],[165.58,165.72],[165.72,166.13],[166.13,166.34],[166.34,166.48],[166.48,166.83],[166.83,167.18],[167.18,167.46],[167.46,167.88]]}]}